  "_doc": "The axes a person's body and face vary along, each one or two pinned CC0 MakeHuman hm08 graphical targets (assets/authored/humans/makehuman_hm08/SOURCE-variation.json). tools/human_variation_kit.py turns them into one shared delta kit over the hm08 body (assets/humans/web/hm08_variation_kit.*); renderers/web/js/human-variation.js draws each person's values from a seed of their own id. `spread` is the standard deviation of the seeded value on the axis's -1..1 scale (a draw is clipped to +-`limit`: MakeHuman's own sliders at 1 are caricature). `scope` says who gets an axis: `face` is everyone, including a seated driver whose clothes and seat were fitted to his body; `full` is only a person on foot, whose garments are carried by the same deltas. No axis value, height or age drawn here is a record fact; a person whose face is fitted to a picture carries fixed values in hm08_variation_persons.json instead, graded by that picture. An asset's `face_bias` (T-3434) is added to every draw of a person wearing that body, before any fitted face: the women's bodies lean their drawn faces toward MakeHuman's own feminine proportions and a resting mouth (`rest` axes are never drawn, only biased), a reconstructed depiction choice, not a record fact.",
